# Each other in Russian: друг друга
subtitle: "Each other in Russian: друг дру́га, друг дру́гу, друг с дру́гом, the -ся of мы ви́делись, and с ним, с ней, с ни́ми."
tags: ["russian","друг друга","each other in russian","russian grammar","new year"]
teaches: ["grammar/reciprocal","vocabulary/family"]
thumb: "band \"Each other: where does the с go?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Passive in Russian: билеты продаются, каток открывается","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/142-russian-passive-sya.cast"}

## Each other in Russian: друг друга
